! ax4b_5b_immediate_unindexed.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148
! (1248, "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113), TEST 5B: "CHKS P
! FIELD OF 100" / "IMMEDIATE MODE, Z TO LA TEST" -- the UNINDEXED
! companion of ax4b_148_immediate_indexed.strap (the block right after
! it in the listing):
!
!   PDF p.143  010767.40-011016.40  driver + error entries, bits 0-5
!   PDF p.144  011017.00-011040.40  error entries, bits 6-14
!   PDF p.145  011041.00-011066.40  entries 15-23, exit, continuity
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013103.00  the common bit table, BIT0-BIT23
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and the
! listing's octal location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi, the
! driver again at 400 dpi; checked row for row against the printed
! machine code by tests/verify_ax4b_5b_immediate_unindexed_listing.py
! (150 rows, 8 symbols, all pass).
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  For k = 0..23:
!   LX,$X3,BITk (address SVA'd in)   $X3 := BITk, one bit of 24 set
!   SVA,$X3,$+.32                    $X3's value INTO THE ADDRESS FIELD
!                                    of the next instruction:
!   LI(BU,64,8),0      0.00 80 400000.20 50   at 010773.40, "F"
!                                    a FULL-WORD VFL at an ODD half-word,
!                                    I = 0, P = 4 (immediate): the 24-bit
!                                    address becomes the operand, zeros
!                                    to the right (printed p.56)
!   LX,$X3,$R; KV,$X3,BITk; BXE      read it back and compare.
! Every bit of the 24-bit address field must survive SVA (24 bits for a
! VFL target, Reference Manual p.29 "Address Insertion") and the
! immediate.  "Z,$X0" opens each pass: a Store Zero into index register
! 0 ("Z TO LA").
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44,
!     read in the page image), so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the
!     error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248 is SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10).
!     The continuity rows after B,SSW are transcribed and verified but
!     never run (SSW halts).
!   * The comment "FROM I4438" between entries 0 and 1 is the page's
!     own (sic: the table is reached from I4838).
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..),
!     as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing
!     else changed.
!
! RESULT ON THE MODEL, 2026-11-18 (a57832f + this deck): PASSES -- halts
! at SSW (PC 1410), SEN = 0, $X1 = BIT23's address 013103.00 with count
! 0, $X2 = entry 23 (011061.00), $X3's value = BIT23's (.01).  CYCLES
! 6721 (6834 before A7 part 2, 2026-11-28: the branch timing) is MODEL
! BEHAVIOUR; no time is printed.  IBM's listing and the
! model AGREE: no finding against the model.
!
! INJECTIONS, each in a scratch copy of bsv/ (the worktree untouched),
! all five routine-148 decks run under each -- OBSERVED for this deck:
!   immediateOperand drops EA bits 18-23 -> FAIL halt (PC 1416), SEN 011050.00
!     (the bit-18 entry of I4839), CYCLES 5398.
!   SVA stores {x.addr[23:5], 5'b0} (bits 19-23 of the value lost) -> FAIL
!     halt, SEN 011052.00 (the bit-19 entry), CYCLES 5680.
!   instrStored forced False (no store-into-prepared hold) -> NO EFFECT, PASS
!     at 6834: this deck does NOT reach that hold; no claim is made for it.
!   P = 0 treated as immediate, X0 writes dropped, I = 0 indexed by X0, FP
!     unnormalized, FP 18-bit rounding, LR into J+1:
!     no effect on PC, SEN or CYCLES here (the driver compared only those;
!     each is caught by a sibling deck).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model, the pins below (PASS, SEN = 0).
!   Each built in a scratch copy of bsv/ and restored (cmp IDENTICAL).
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
! The addresses are the ones this listing prints for them (SIC,SEN
! "1310.00 80", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80", B,SSW
! "1301.10 00"), the same as routine 148's; what is AT them is SSIP's,
! which this file replaces with halts, as ax4b_148_immediate_indexed does.
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, the continuity word: SYN from the printed address of
! "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32 10); the three continuity rows that name it
! are never reached here (SSW halts first).
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.143, 010767.40-011016.40 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)10767.40
I4836A  LVI, $X1, BIT0                ! -TEST 5B CHKS P FIELD OF 100.
        LVI, $X2, I4839               ! -IMMEDIATE MODE, Z TO LA TEST.
        LCI, $X1, 24
I4837   Z,   $X0
        SVA, $X2, I4838
        SVA, $X1, $+.32
        LX,  $X3, 0
        SVA, $X3, $+.32
        LI(BU,64,8), 0
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        LX,  $X3, $R
        SVA, $X1, $+.32
        KV,  $X3, 0
        BXE, $+1.0
I4838   $B,  0                        ! -FAILURE
!
I4838A  C-I, $X1, 1                   ! -SEE IF DONE.
        BXCZ, I4840
        V+I, $X1, 1.0
        V+I, $X2, 2.0
        BD,  I4837
        CNOP
!
! error table: PDF p.143 (bits 0-5), p.144 (bits 6-14), p.145 (15-23)
I4839   SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 0.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
!                                     ! -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM I4438
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 1.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 2.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 3.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 4.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 5.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
! ---- PDF p.144, 011017.00-011040.40 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 6.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 7.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 8.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 9.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 10.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 11.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 12.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 13.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 14.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
! ---- PDF p.145, 011041.00-011066.40 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 15.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 16.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 17.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 18.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 19.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 20.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 21.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 22.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LOAD IMMEDIATE FAILURE,BIT 23.
        B,   SERS
        B,   I4838A
        NOP
!
I4840   B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4836A
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
        LX,  $X13, IC248              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY.
        V+,  $X13, BIT22
        SX,  $X13, IC248
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.191, 013054.00-013103.00: the common bit table, BIT0-BIT23
! (the page continues to BIT35; BIT24, a DD, and BIT25 up are not used)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)13054.0
BIT0   XW,  (8)400000.00, 0, 0
BIT1   XW,  (8)200000.00, 0, 0
BIT2   XW,  (8)100000.00, 0, 0
BIT3   XW,  (8)40000.00, 0, 0
BIT4   XW,  (8)20000.00, 0, 0
BIT5   XW,  (8)10000.00, 0, 0
BIT6   XW,  (8)4000.00, 0, 0
BIT7   XW,  (8)2000.00, 0, 0
BIT8   XW,  (8)1000.00, 0, 0
BIT9   XW,  (8)400.00, 0, 0
BIT10  XW,  (8)200.00, 0, 0
BIT11  XW,  (8)100.00, 0, 0
BIT12  XW,  (8)40.00, 0, 0
BIT13  XW,  (8)20.00, 0, 0
BIT14  XW,  (8)10.00, 0, 0
BIT15  XW,  (8)4.00, 0, 0
BIT16  XW,  (8)2.00, 0, 0
BIT17  XW,  (8)1.00, 0, 0
BIT18  XW,  (8).40, 0, 0
BIT19  XW,  (8).20, 0, 0
BIT20  XW,  (8).10, 0, 0
BIT21  XW,  (8)0.04, 0, 0
BIT22  XW,  (8)0.02, 0, 0
BIT23  XW,  (8)0.01, 0, 0
        END, I4836A
